WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.720
- [Mark] All right, Heather.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.553
- Yes.

00:00:04.553 --> 00:00:05.386
- [Mark] Heather. Oh, where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:06.388
Where are you from originally?

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:07.540
- [Heather] Originally,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.973
I'm from Detroit, Michigan.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.850
I grew up in Brooklyn, New York.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.096
And now I'm in Los Angeles.

00:00:15.096 --> 00:00:17.060
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.910
- I have a big Italian family,

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.680
and most of them are still in New York.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.393
We are from Sicily, originally.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.710
And, basically I have three
sisters and one brother,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:29.202
and a single mother.

00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:33.067
- [Mark] How would you
describe your childhood?

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.220
- Turmoil.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.510
My mother was an alcoholic,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.880
and I basically took care
of my two younger siblings.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.840
And she was abusive.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.093
So, it was hectic at most.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.920
- [Mark] What kind of abuse?

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.753
- Physical.

00:00:51.705 --> 00:00:53.070
She drank a lot.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.060
And became very violent.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.470
And because I was the
only one in the house,

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.483
I was the target of that violence.

00:01:03.191 --> 00:01:04.580
- [Mark] And you went through high school?

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.120
- I did, but I did not graduate.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.953
I went to...

00:01:07.953 --> 00:01:10.570
I left my house when I was 16

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.403
with Job Corps.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.000
I graduated from Job Corps

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.363
and got married at 17.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.968
And had four children.

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:19.801
- [Mark] You have four kids?

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.316
- Yes.

00:01:21.316 --> 00:01:23.700
- [Mark] And you raise them?

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.580
- I did up until my oldest was 13

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.613
and they got removed from my care.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.390
- [Mark] How did that go about?

00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:39.240
- I just had a lot of baggage.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.987
I came out here and...

00:01:40.987 --> 00:01:42.437
- [Mark] How is the marriage?

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.253
- It wasn't good.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.290
I mean, I was 17.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:53.180
My mom pretty much gave me away to him.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.310
He was 23 years old.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:59.317
And wasn't a good marriage at all.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:03.240
But, I had nowhere else
to go, so I stayed.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.753
- [Mark] What kind of stuff
went on in the marriage?

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.033
- A lot of abuse.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.343
He was just very abusive.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.430
- [Mark] So physical?

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.950
- Yeah. And mentally

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.313
Oh.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.090
It was just not,

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.250
you shouldn't get married at 17.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.540
You are not even an adult at the age.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.373
And,

00:02:32.962 --> 00:02:34.060
- [Mark] Is that what
got you to come to LA?

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:34.896
- Yes.

00:02:34.896 --> 00:02:36.146
- [Mark] Okay.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.083
- I left.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:50.900
I think I was 20, 23, 24
years old, when I left

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:54.803
and came out here

00:02:54.803 --> 00:02:55.883
didn't know anybody.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.800
Wanting to get far away

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.820
and stayed at the mission,

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.810
the Union Rescue Mission.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.740
And that's when my children
got removed from me.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.630
And that's when I started
with the drug abuse.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:15.973
I was on Hydrocodone since I
was 17 because I have Lupus.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.770
So, they basically just said,

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.160
you have a terminal illness

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.770
and we're gonna make you
as comfortable as possible.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.293
So they put me on
Hydrocodone at 17 years old.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.680
I go through 80 pills in two weeks.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.860
At this point, because my body has built

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:37.290
up such an immune system that I can't...

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.080
it doesn't take full effect with me.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.320
And without those pills,
I go through withdrawals.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.150
And when I go through withdrawals

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.180
and I can't get the hydrocodone,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.520
I started seeing a man out here,

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.670
and he was on sherm.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.750
I didn't know what sherm was,

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.860
never did it before.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.393
And, so I started with the sherm.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:07.160
At first, it was every now and again,

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.633
when I didn't have my pills.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.100
And then it got more frequent

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.653
because just like the
pills it is addictive.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:21.520
I got to a point where
I almost got kicked out

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.770
of my apartment when I lived over at...

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.380
'cause I used to live over here

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.380
where my friend Gigi stays now

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.250
and I almost got kicked out

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.840
because me and him were doing it so much.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.220
It puts you in a daze
where you really don't know

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.250
what you're doing.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:44.610
You're almost stagnant,
because you're so high

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.433
you stay frozen or you just freak out.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.743
It puts you in a
different type of reality.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:56.900
Recently, I did it and I
was staying at the Hayward

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.060
and I was out front
because he's not allowed

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.163
in the building anymore
because of our drug use.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.040
And I was so high that
I really thought that

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.200
I was in this like daze
that I thought that

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.630
the world was coming to an end.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.330
I just had this foreboding feeling

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.380
and I kinda flipped out.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.920
And I ran away from him.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.860
And just a lot of things
could have happened to me.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.430
But thank God that they didn't.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:26.723
Because I was so high.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.480
Because without my hydrocodone,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.930
that's the only thing that
helps with my withdrawals.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.650
I get very sick when I don't have them.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:40.650
And, as sometimes I go back to my doctor

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.300
and try to get more and he supplies it.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.850
So I take 'em.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:49.040
I mean, I've been taking
them since I was 17

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.020
and there's no way I can stop
taking them at this point.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.330
Because if I don't, I get sick.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.120
And I need a substitute.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.020
And sherm's my substitute

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.680
and I can't stop because
without it, I get ill.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.730
Like right now I ran out.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:09.730
And, I'm trying to get
enough money to get sherm.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.513
That's what I do.

00:06:12.513 --> 00:06:13.407
- [Mark] So, the pills are your preference

00:06:13.407 --> 00:06:15.160
or is it the sherm?

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.350
- The pill's my preference

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.100
but when I don't have them,

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.007
I go to sherm.

00:06:19.007 --> 00:06:19.840
- Right.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.230
- I've done crystal before,

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:27.920
but I can't do that because it
makes my heart race too much.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.993
And I become short of breath.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.390
My Lupus,

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.223
it seems like

00:06:34.223 --> 00:06:37.650
with the pills, has attacked my body more.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.400
I've had a kidney removed.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.760
I've been on dialysis

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.803
and I don't stop because I can't.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.360
I have to have them.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.040
I mean, there's no other...

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.590
there's nothing else
more to say I have to.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:55.590
My body now is so addicted to
them that if I don't take it

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:56.923
I will be ill.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.860
Regardless how it's affected my body,

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.610
regardless how it's affected my Lupus.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.620
I do have seizures.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.943
I've had seizures when I took in sherm.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.990
And I still do.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:10.823
I have to.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.230
- [Mark] And your kids are where?

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.240
- They're in foster care.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.890
They actually got adopted out.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.633
I do see my 18 year
old daughter sometimes.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:22.650
She knows that there's a difference in me,

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.340
but she doesn't know the reason

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.790
I did not share this with her.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:26.763
And I won't.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:32.683
It's just depression on
top of everything else.

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:36.723
It's my only escape from reality.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.323
So, I do it.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.803
And there is no stopping.

00:07:43.905 --> 00:07:45.448
- [Mark] And how are you
supporting yourself now?

00:07:45.448 --> 00:07:46.448
- I get SSI.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.233
I use that money to support my habit.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.180
I get pills from my doctor.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:59.273
He supplies the the hydrocodone.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:02.140
80 pills are gone within two weeks,

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.123
sometimes a week.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.810
Because I take them constantly.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:08.180
Because I'm so immune to them now

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.943
I have to take at least eight
in one day, if not more.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.603
And it's causing problems with my liver,

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.103
but, I can't stop.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.523
And I'm not going to.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.150
I have to, I have to, it's a need.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.253
I have to take them.

00:08:26.174 --> 00:08:28.600
Because if I don't, like
I said, I get very ill.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:29.850
I go through withdrawals,

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:34.040
and with everything else,

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.757
I don't want to be sick.

00:08:35.757 --> 00:08:37.707
- [Mark] Looking at your situation now.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.103
What do you think?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.660
What would you point a finger at to...

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:44.610
- The doctors.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:49.000
Because, instead of caring for my illness,

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.530
they pretty much gave up on me and said,

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.580
I'm just gonna make her
comfortable until she dies.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:57.900
They gave me to the age of
45 before my body gives out.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.950
So, at this point,

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.130
I'm basically saying,

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.240
well I'm gonna die anyway.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.593
So, I might as well be comfortable.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.313
So that's why I do it.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:12.150
The doctors, they don't care.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.900
Especially when you
have a terminal illness

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.750
all they want to do is
make you comfortable.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.583
And that's it.

00:09:16.583 --> 00:09:19.510
They don't really check to
see how your condition is.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.223
They don't see you deteriorating.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.440
And you take it as they don't care.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:25.543
So why should you?

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:29.620
- [Mark] This has gotta be
impressing for you, right?

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.503
- It is very.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.837
And that just makes me want to do it more.

00:09:33.837 --> 00:09:35.070
- [Mark] Right.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:39.283
Because I feel like, if nobody
else cares, why should I?

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:45.080
So I do it and I'm going
to continue doing it

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:48.243
because if I'm going to die,
I'm not gonna be in pain.

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:54.053
I feel bad because,

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:56.483
my children.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.810
when they do come of age and I'm not here.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.683
I wonder what people say about me.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.203
What they will hear.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.883
But the same time,

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.290
I don't want to be in pain.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.443
I've gone through enough of that.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:21.870
My body has betrayed me.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:23.130
I feel so...

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.930
And then on top of that, I
feel like I'm just alone.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.553
So, why not make myself comfortable?

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:35.923
Why not ease that pain?

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.640
Cause I'm in constant pain

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.600
from the lupus and seizures.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.190
People don't understand.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:45.840
They don't know what
lupus does to a person.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.770
Especially when you
have it since you're 17.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.660
You have organs being removed,

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.533
because the lupus is attacking it.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.810
And you're in constant pain.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.563
And the doctors don't care.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.420
And all they want to do is

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.620
hear shove some pills

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.563
and take these and buy.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.580
They don't even check to
see how your condition is

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.120
until something comes so severe

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.173
that an organ has to be removed.

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.457
And to me, they failed me.

00:11:13.893 --> 00:11:15.680
- [Mark] Do you ever look at the

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:18.120
childhood abuse that you endured

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:21.590
and then the marriage that you had,

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:22.960
and how that kind of...

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:24.307
- That, affects me a lot.

00:11:24.307 --> 00:11:25.774
- [Mark] Created a whole
series of problems.

00:11:25.774 --> 00:11:26.620
- Yes.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:30.043
Not with just the drug abuse,
but with relationships.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.420
The one that I was doing
sherm with was abusive.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:37.610
I almost got shot in the
head because we were so high

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:38.900
and he was playing with a gun

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.810
and it got this much close to my head.

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.823
And I could have died.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:45.920
And we were just so high.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:47.023
I just didn't care.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:56.710
It's just, a lot to take
in just for one person.

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.030
Not just to mention with my health issues,

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.523
with my family.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.150
I'm very distant with them.

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.860
I don't really talk to them.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:07.760
I'm not close with them.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.780
So I'm pretty much alone.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:11.610
My children were the only thing I had.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:13.460
And when they took that away from me,

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.193
I just didn't care anymore.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:22.730
So, I just take as many
pills as I need to.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.470
And, when I don't have them,

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.573
I go to sherm.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.570
I've done cocaine before.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:31.610
It doesn't do anything to me because,

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.460
I guess my metabolism is so used to

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.393
the high amounts of hydrocodone.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:41.630
It really other drugs don't affect me.

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:42.463
Other than sherm

00:12:42.463 --> 00:12:43.893
because of what sherm is.

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:48.830
So, basically it's just those two things.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.320
I've tried other things because,

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.550
I wanted a different outlet,

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.290
and it doesn't work with me.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.410
- [Mark] sherm is PCP?

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:57.330
- Yes.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.500
- And is that a good substitute

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.111
for the pills that you can't afford?

00:13:00.111 --> 00:13:00.944
- Yes.

00:13:00.944 --> 00:13:02.713
Because of how strong it is.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.410
It makes the pain go away.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:09.050
It doesn't last very long as the pills do.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.410
But it lasts as long enough

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:12.240
for me to forget that I'm in pain.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.520
- [Mark] You smoke it, right?

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.250
- Yes. So a cigarette is basically liquid

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.090
in a very small capsule.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:21.640
And you take the cigarette
and you dip it in the bottle

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:22.800
and you smoke it.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.453
And that's how it's adjusted.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:28.280
And then shortly after that,

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.200
you go through a whole like

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.840
anesthesia moment where you you feel like

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:38.110
you're in a different realm

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:41.090
or your mind just wanders,

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:42.800
but it can be very dangerous

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.830
because you you're like
almost stagnant or frozen.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:47.990
Your whole body.

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.320
Everything's frozen.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:50.688
There was a time that I've done it.

00:13:50.688 --> 00:13:52.820
And I was in an elevator
for like 20 minutes

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.880
because, I didn't realize I was there.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.010
You basically, your body is frozen

00:13:58.010 --> 00:13:59.990
your mind's somewhere else.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:03.520
So, you kind of escape your whole body

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.900
and you go to a different state of mind.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:06.750
- [Mark] And I'm sure you see that

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.420
you're in a very self-destructive...

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.700
- [Heather] Yes.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.543
But, at this point in time,

00:14:13.664 --> 00:14:15.420
I don't care.

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:18.500
Because, everyone else has given up on me

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.603
that it made me give up on myself.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.073
And I feel as though that's
the only thing that's

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:29.570
I can actually turn to at this time.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:34.240
And, it's the only thing
that's kind of getting me

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:39.230
out of my thoughts and
taking me somewhere else.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:40.810
I have a pain out of all

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.930
thinking about all this
stuff that I think about.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.617
- [Mark] Yeah, but being apart
from your kids must be...

00:14:45.617 --> 00:14:47.630
That'd be enough to
break any woman, right?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.463
- [Mark] Yes.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:50.880
- [Heather] It's the only thing that's

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.056
taking my mind off that.

00:14:53.056 --> 00:14:54.500
- [Mark] Do you still talk to your kids?

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.103
- [Heather] No. Only
my oldest daughter 18.

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:01.183
I haven't talked to my
children in almost four years.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:08.750
My oldest son is 20 and doesn't
want anything to do with me.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:11.143
He was taken from me when he was 14.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.170
And now he's 20.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.217
And then my daughter.

00:15:16.217 --> 00:15:19.180
- [Mark] So the drug use
started for you at what age?

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.573
- [Heather] My drug use started at 23.

00:15:22.481 --> 00:15:23.314
- [Mark] And how old are you now?

00:15:23.314 --> 00:15:25.010
- [Heather] I'm 39.

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:26.130
- [Mark] So when your kids were young

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:27.920
you were playing around with drugs too.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:28.860
- [Heather] Yeah.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.163
Because of the pain that I was in.

00:15:33.499 --> 00:15:35.853
I was on the pills before
I even had children.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:39.100
And when they were born,

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.400
I didn't stop taking them.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:42.880
I continued to take them.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.360
I didn't really start the sherm until

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.810
after they were taken though.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.960
I was only here a few months

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.110
before they were taken.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:58.030
And right after that, I
was introduced to sherm.

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:01.960
And that's when that began
and I have not stopped yet.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:04.040
It's been about five or six years now

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.290
since I've been doing it.

00:16:08.757 --> 00:16:10.310
- [Mark] What's the biggest mistake?

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:11.660
What's your biggest regret?

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:16.240
- Getting married at the young
age that I was married in.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.030
Having children with the wrong man

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:21.293
and coming out here.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.910
Because before this,

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:27.133
other than the pills,

00:16:28.836 --> 00:16:31.070
I had no interest in doing different drugs

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:31.903
and things like that.

00:16:31.903 --> 00:16:35.590
And then I came out here, things happened

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.563
and I went full force.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.913
Not caring about the consequences.

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:44.950
I still, at this point don't care

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.713
because I just feel like,

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.093
with a terminal illness that I have,

00:16:54.778 --> 00:16:58.750
I rather die not being in pain

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:02.170
and not being depressed all the time.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:04.070
Than, to be in pain

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:07.590
and to be hurt emotionally.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:09.123
Who wants to die like that?

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.993
So, that's why I do it.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.690
- [Mark] What is the most
important thing you've learned

00:17:21.664 --> 00:17:22.831
in your life?

00:17:24.413 --> 00:17:26.363
- I don't even think I've learned it yet.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:30.750
I don't think I've learned it yet.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:31.583
To be honest.

00:17:31.583 --> 00:17:32.416
Because if I did,

00:17:32.416 --> 00:17:33.710
I wouldn't be doing these drugs, right?

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:34.543
- [Mark] Right.

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:36.850
- I haven't learned it yet.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.700
And hopefully it will.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.453
I know I'm being self-destructive.

00:17:44.577 --> 00:17:46.203
I acknowledge that.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:51.950
But, with everything that happens to me,

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:53.823
or have had had happened to me,

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.990
you come to a point
where you just give up.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.837
And I think that's what I did.

00:18:04.123 --> 00:18:04.956
I gave up.

00:18:06.195 --> 00:18:09.440
Gave up on myself and on my life.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:13.180
There is no going back from that.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:17.660
You get in so deep emotionally

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.760
and physically that there's a point where

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.083
you can't come back from it.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:30.990
And, I think I've reached that point.

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:34.132
I've actually tried to commit suicide

00:18:34.132 --> 00:18:35.560
more than once.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:36.910
Because I couldn't take it.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.053
It just wouldn't stick, I guess.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:48.163
So, I guess I'm just
self-destructive this way.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.143
And there's no coming back from it.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:55.823
So I do what I do.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.343
I'm just hoping that when I am gone,

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:05.310
my children will learn about who I was

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.430
when they wasn't around.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.520
That's my only hope.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:11.720
And that's my only regret is that

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:14.180
they find out

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:17.223
how their mother screwed up so much.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:20.190
- [Mark] What would you say to your kids,

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:21.253
if God forbid,

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:23.980
something like that happened.

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:27.226
And your kids watch this video

00:19:27.226 --> 00:19:28.059
- That.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.763
it's not their fault.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.253
And.

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:38.551
That I left them.

00:19:38.551 --> 00:19:40.900
And I never wanted this to happen.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.167
But it did.

00:19:42.167 --> 00:19:44.000
And you have choices.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.350
You have to live with those choices.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:48.473
And hopefully they make the right ones.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:50.200
Because I didn't.

00:19:53.793 --> 00:19:55.473
And I can't go back.

00:19:59.729 --> 00:20:00.562
- [Mark] All right, Heather.

00:20:00.562 --> 00:20:02.120
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.277
- Thank you.

00:20:03.277 --> 00:20:04.177
- [Mark] I wish you lots of luck.

00:20:04.177 --> 00:20:05.247
- Thank you.

00:20:12.647 --> 00:20:14.170
- [Mark] Are you going
to the women's center?

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:15.940
Over at 5th and San Pedro?

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:16.773
- [Heather] No.

00:20:16.773 --> 00:20:21.170
- [Mark] You didn't want to go over there.

